`cache-push-darwin.yml` is deleted. It ran on a GitHub-hosted `macos-14`
runner because the fleet has no darwin machine, and in 299 runs it never
concluded success once — 271 cancelled, 26 failed. It never created
`cache-ready-darwin`, so nothing has ever pinned that ref.

Nothing regresses, because nothing was being delivered. What a mac can
substitute is the Linux→Darwin cross closure, and the linux lane already
realises and publishes every one of those roots from
`cachePushRoots.x86_64-linux`. Darwin consumers pin `cache-ready`, the same
ref the rest of the fleet tracks.

What a mac now builds locally is the set of genuinely native
`aarch64-darwin` roots with no cross story yet — Apple-framework packages
(`ghostty`, `vmkit`, `screencast`), the repo's own Rust CLIs, and the site
and Python trees. That was already true in practice; it is now true by
declaration. `#3586` tracks moving each of them onto the cross lane, at
which point they publish through the linux lane like `btop`, `codex` and
`nix-ix` already do.

The removal also takes the last GitHub-hosted Nix installer with it, so no
lane in this repo installs Determinate Nix any more.
